## B) BDM insights (added during our work — keep these)

### How to work with Daniel

- Trust but verify. Other AIs already crashed his live site with bad code.
  Check every snippet against existing Additional CSS and `tc-` classes.
- One problem at a time. Exact clicks. Screenshots welcome.
- Protect energy: cosmetic bugs are not launch blockers.
- Prefer patterns, global styles, and reusable HTML over editing dozens of pages.
- Size judgment: his 4K laptop + Windows scale + per-site zoom fools him.
  Use Incognito at 100% (Ctrl+0); compare to Medium.com if needed.
- When context is full: finish the in-flight task, then new chat with
  HANDOFF.md pasted.

### Image / CSS failure modes already paid for

- Never paste global CSS that overrides `.tc-overlay-card` / `.tc-explore-hub`
  with overflow visible, height auto, or object-fit contain. Remove wrong
  classes from wrong blocks instead.
- Match class to job: hover crop card ≠ banner ≠ hero ≠ book ≠ editorial B&W.
  Wrong class is the main crop cause, not Canva size.
- Books: `tc-book-card` + `tc-leadership-body` + `tc-book-button` only.
  Never overlay/explore on book covers.
- Never stack `tc-explore-banner` with overlay/hub. Append scoped CSS blocks;
  do not casually rewrite locked earlier blocks.
- Missing EXPLORE with hover still working: often `kb-section-link-overlay`
  covering the ::after pill — link the image or turn off Section Link.
- Check Kadence “Use fixed ratio” and Gutenberg Wide/Full before blaming CSS.
- Additive safe classes: `tc-explore-banner`, `tc-bw-reveal`, membership
  toggle namespace (`tc-membership`, `tc-toggle`, etc.).

### Membership, hosting, other AIs

- Email-only unlock via MailerLite. No passwords unless Daniel explicitly asks.
  Recommended template: `membership-toggle/page-templates/page-0-email-unlock.html`.
- Never recommend Tailwind, replatform, or rebuild from scratch.
- Vet other AIs and builder claims (especially 10Web AI regenerate) against
  custom-code risk. Migrate tcstaging → verify `.10web.site` → then DNS.
- Do not download multi-GB backups to his laptop. Good site folder is
  `public_html/tcstaging`, not the older `staging`.
